# Local cruft from in-place editing on the host.
*.bak
*.save
*.log
*.orig
*.new

# Credential and deployment-parameter files. NOTHING of this shape is ever
# tracked. The rule is broad on purpose: these apps keep Usenet provider logins
# and indexer API keys in their own config files, and the realistic way one gets
# published is copying it here to look at during debugging. Compose also reads
# .env automatically from the project directory.
*.env
.env
config.xml
sabnzbd.ini
secrets.env

# `install` additionally refuses to run if it finds a credential-shaped file in
# this directory, because no pattern list catches every name someone might use.
